      "filename": "dheeraj_s_roy_autumn_arons_teryn_i_mitchell_michele_pignatelli_tomás_j_ryan_susumu_tonegawa_memory_retrieval_by_activating_engram_cells_in_mouse_models_of_early_alzheimers_disease.md",
      "summary": "This document presents a study conducted by the RIKEN-MIT Center for Neural Circuit Genetics on memory retrieval in early Alzheimer's disease using mouse models. The research primarily investigates the potential of activating engram cells as a method for memory retrieval in the early stages of the disease. The document is a detailed 26-page PDF, relevant to those interested in neuroscience, Alzheimer's research, and memory retrieval techniques.",
