      "filename": "xiao_zhou_rex_n_tien_sadhana_ravikumar_and_steven_m_chase_distinct_types_of_neural_reorganization_during_long-term_learning.md",
      "summary": "The document \"Distinct types of neural reorganization during long-term learning\" is a research study by Xiao Zhou, Rex N. Tien, Sadhana Ravikumar, and Steven M. Chase. The study, conducted at Carnegie Mellon University, focuses on the various types of neural reorganization that take place during long-term learning. The document is a 13-page PDF and is part of a literature review in neuroscience.",
