    "/home/batesk52/CMU.49.007-Literature-Review/document_summaries/by_type/pdfs/josh_berke_what_does_dopamine_mean_1.md": {
      "file_path": "/home/batesk52/CMU.49.007-Literature-Review/document_summaries/by_type/pdfs/josh_berke_what_does_dopamine_mean_1.md",
      "relative_path": "/home/batesk52/CMU.49.007-Literature-Review/document_summaries/by_type/pdfs/josh_berke_what_does_dopamine_mean_1.md",
      "filename": "josh_berke_what_does_dopamine_mean_1.md",
      "summary": "The document is an in-depth exploration of dopamine's role and significance, authored by Josh Berke from the University of California. The primary focus is on dopamine's function as a crucial modulator of learning and motivation, with a particular interest in how target cells interpret increased dopamine signals. This suggests a complex understanding of this neurotransmitter's function.",
